The transition to a living initiative began as curators and community members sought a way to keep Odeh‚Äôs legacy alive beyond the physical risks inherent in a single, static object. During a 2023 residency at the Grand Central Art Center in Santa Ana, artist Jon Rubin began working with the community to reframe the memorial‚Äôs purpose. Rubin explained that rather than focusing on a fixed monument, the project emphasizes decentralization, turning the responsibility of memory into a collective conversation. This approach involves a series of dinners, performances, and public gatherings hosted by various individuals and organizations. By inviting people into a space of hospitality and shared dialogue, the initiative aims to build inter-community justice and peace, embodying the values Odeh himself was invested in promoting. This evolution invites a community to hold the memory of an activist not in bronze, but in the ongoing relationships and practices of those who participate in the work.ÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tngKzsTUODjbjVcYEiBcyrSxiHmTTXPSXLFHNvX4oQgÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkxRmnProseContributionSettlementÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;j4Jg92g0mnid8H7J4stwTFlIFHp4Unxg94J17EV5yjYÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx9ni:///sha-256;5iOWtyn85BjWimcxvVvXZ9D9uAsvIiij6l_40RsZlSEÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;pAaoIvX7-hI9FsX45GwNQ1KVnjlEzjlqUI8xQ2BL4ScÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkx$https://koios.news/activitypub/actorÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;fliJ0co3uDMphLI11_4WlLpD7pByq9X5GmilKikcHmEÉdpairÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉerightÅdunitÉdleftÅdstarÅdunitÇdmarkfAcceptÉdpairÉhconstantÇdbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;uXMyRlKXByfDvxEiwiHpMRHNljUh0qR